From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OneFeiFan <3022504358@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: idle entry fixes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This patch consolidates the following patches of the r16 series
(original authors are kept in the attached commit messages):

- 旧 0050：cpuidle: Don't return from inside __CPU_PM_CPU_IDLE_ENTER() macro（Sultan Alsawaf）
- 旧 0051：cpuidle: Reject idle entry if need_resched() is true（Sultan Alsawaf）

Origin: 上游 1ebbdf5c22、1d2ce9dee1（经 ztc1997）（旧 0050、0051）
Upstream-Status: Backport
KABI: none
Depends-On: none
Notes: 旧 0050 + 0051 合并
Tested-On: r16（2026-11-01）：完整构建、KMI 门禁（7298 个导出符号，缺失 0，CRC 差异 0；670 个厂商模块 0 失败）、开机

Original commit messages:

----- 旧 0050：cpuidle: Don't return from inside __CPU_PM_CPU_IDLE_ENTER() macro -----
Author: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>

Altering control flow from inside a macro is a recipe for disaster. This is
a nightmare for readability and makes it very easy to trip over the return
nestled in the __CPU_PM_CPU_IDLE_ENTER() macro.

Restructure __CPU_PM_CPU_IDLE_ENTER() to eliminate the nasty return.

Signed-off-by: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>

----- 旧 0051：cpuidle: Reject idle entry if need_resched() is true -----
Author: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>

There's no reason to enter idle at this point in __CPU_PM_CPU_IDLE_ENTER()
if the CPU needs to reschedule. Instead of fruitlessly entering the
architecture's idle routine, reject the idle entry attempt with an error as
an optimization.

Signed-off-by: Sultan Alsawaf <sultan@kerneltoast.com>
---
 include/linux/cpuidle.h | 19 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/cpuidle.h b/include/linux/cpuidle.h
index 4b51019dd..b9f28bf17 100644
--- a/include/linux/cpuidle.h
+++ b/include/linux/cpuidle.h
@@ -286,17 +286,18 @@ extern s64 cpuidle_governor_latency_req(unsigned int cpu);
 ({									\
 	int __ret = 0;							\
 									\
-	if (!idx) {							\
+	if (need_resched()) {						\
+		__ret = -1;						\
+	} else if (!idx) {						\
 		cpu_do_idle();						\
-		return idx;						\
-	}								\
-									\
-	if (!is_retention)						\
-		__ret =  cpu_pm_enter();				\
-	if (!__ret) {							\
-		__ret = low_level_idle_enter(state);			\
+	} else {							\
 		if (!is_retention)					\
-			cpu_pm_exit();					\
+			__ret = cpu_pm_enter();				\
+		if (!__ret) {						\
+			__ret = low_level_idle_enter(state);		\
+			if (!is_retention)				\
+				cpu_pm_exit();				\
+		}							\
 	}								\
 									\
 	__ret ? -1 : idx;						\
